ion":"1788409047479971001-a8d2a7b5-8a86-4b10-8ee4-081455d91d8d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9e1b6ee9b079db9a336486851302ecc24ec8bc3420eb478c4f4d803d0b2385bb","event_uuid":"0da95640-f780-4ebe-9df0-986b2d5960af","position":{"commit_sha":"dc96b54f7759f820738b6d75b596edfdcaa47e40","position":"1788410143755207001-0da95640-f780-4ebe-9df0-986b2d5960af"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b4eeae8962710ace1fb2716900fd6fada0f434321a1268f17ba57c02de34ffc9","event_uuid":"99556c04-24ce-46d5-8709-c2ec37c8b6f3","position":{"commit_sha":"7697d045627e601a689b9b37635b9c91a0cc6e78","position":"1788410150666379001-99556c04-24ce-46d5-8709-c2ec37c8b6f3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Handoff state. Implemented and pushed as Gerrit change 2537 (\"Derive the op-cert kind vocabulary\"). Gate state at handoff: LLM-Review +1, Verified -1 — the code review PASSED and only CI is red.\n\nTwo failure signatures are open across this stack and neither root cause is confirmed yet:\n1. change 2530 fails the `require resolvable rebar ticket` job, although `rebar resolve` succeeds locally and the trailer is well-formed — the leading hypothesis is that the ticket is not visible to CI (the `tickets` branch may not have reached `origin`);\n2. pytest fails in ~50s on several changes, fast enough to be a collection/import error, and it does NOT reproduce locally.\n\nDo NOT close this ticket until its change is Verified +1 and merged. A subagent is driving the stack to green; a session-only cron loop (46e3b0eb) is harvesting reviews, landing green changes and closing merged tickets.\n\nNote for whoever lands this: amend only with `git commit --amend --no-edit`. Re-committing a change that already carries a Change-Id opens a DUPLICATE Gerrit change — that is how change 2534 came to exist and be abandoned.","timestamp":1788398771671778001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1788317622517845001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"61a5a7f3-fdb6-4d62-bf5e-19dc89330e8a","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f9b9-83ad-931c-4833"},{"link_uuid":"3fa52ef0-d44c-4048-86c7-ef0aa2cebffb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fa96-a687-b41c-45bf"}],"description":"Mirror inventory finding F2 (`reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md`), MEDIUM.\n\n## Problem\n\nThe op-cert kind vocabulary has three masters:\n\n- `src/rebar/signing.py:115` `OPCERT_KINDS` — canonical, and already EXPORTED in `__all__` at `:76`\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:38` `VALID_KINDS` — the same two, hand-copied\n- `src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:24` `_VALID_KINDS` — the same two again, plus a prose copy\n  in `_USAGE` at `:23`\n\nNeither consumer imports the exported name, and both gate client REQUEST VALIDATION: a kind\npresent in `OPCERT_KINDS` but missing from a consumer's copy is silently rejected as invalid.\nChurn is low — ADR 0049 fixes the count at two — which is precisely why a miss would sit\nunnoticed.\n\n## The consumers, and why a naive import would be WRONG\n\n`OPCERT_KINDS` is a `frozenset` — UNORDERED. Both copies are ordered TUPLES, and three\nconsumers depend on that:\n\n- `_cli/_parsers/advanced/certs.py:51` — `choices=remote_cert._VALID_KINDS`. argparse renders\n  `choices` into help and into its error text, so a frozenset makes both non-deterministic.\n- `opcert_service/app.py:222` — `f\"kind must be one of {list(jobs.VALID_KINDS)}\"`, an\n  order-visible API error message.\n- `opcert_service/__init__.py:14,18` — re-exports `VALID_KINDS` in `__all__`. It is PUBLIC\n  API, so changing its type is a breaking change independent of ordering.\n\n(`app.py:217` is a membership test and is indifferent.)\n\n## Approach — generate-from-canonical, preserving type and order\n\nBoth copies become `tuple(sorted(OPCERT_KINDS))`. Sorted order is\n`(\"completion-verifier\", \"plan-review\")` — byte-identical to what both copies hold today, so\nevery consumer above sees exactly what it sees now, while the MEMBERSHIP stops being a\nhand-copy. `_USAGE` prose is generated from the same tuple.\n\nDeriving a frozenset here would have been the wrong fix, and that is the substance of this\nticket: the canonical value and its consumers disagree about whether order is part of the fact.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] AC1: both copies are derived from `signing.OPCERT_KINDS` and neither re-lists the kinds.\n      Verified by a test asserting each equals `tuple(sorted(OPCERT_KINDS))` and the literals are gone.\n- [x] AC1b: both remain ORDERED TUPLES with their current order, so argparse `choices`, the\n      `app.py:222` error message and the `opcert_service.__all__` export are unchanged. Verified by\n      a test asserting the exact tuple value and its type.\n- [x] AC2: `remote_cert`'s `_USAGE` names exactly the canonical kinds, generated not re-typed.\n      Verified by a test comparing the usage text against the set.\n- [x] AC3: a kind added to `OPCERT_KINDS` is accepted by both consumers with no further edit.\n      Verified by a test that patches the canonical set and asserts both validators follow.\n- [x] AC4: an unknown kind is still rejected at both sites. Verified by explicit rejection tests.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `python -m pytest tests/unit -k \"opcert or remote_cert or signing\" -q` — AC1-AC4.\n- `make lint && make typecheck`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py","reason":"import the canonical OPCERT_KINDS"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py","reason":"import the canonical OPCERT_KINDS and generate the usage text"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_kind_vocabulary.py","reason":"the oracle"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f"],["relates_to","fa96-a687-b41c-45bf"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"f79d-0d71-0fd7-439f","parent_status_uuid":"0da95640-f780-4ebe-9df0-986b2d5960af","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6850-af5c-a4a1-4c5d","ticket_type":"task","title":"Single-source the op-cert kinds across signing, opcert_service and remote_cert (mirror F2)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["2c2f6164-7702-45d3-8386-a01c243a501e","80877cc5-0b91-46a6-8218-a72540542396","4f23e397-a3b0-4210-8d5c-5d72db82e490","a1df4ad4-9145-4651-b9e7-360d87678e16","ae42c0d0-2aee-421f-878a-3458fda76beb","0ada822c-565f-4b47-ba3b-bd996e07111c","3fa52ef0-d44c-4048-86c7-ef0aa2cebffb","f5eaac58-cb56-4933-9da0-52592292ab6a","a8d2a7b5-8a86-4b10-8ee4-081455d91d8d","0da95640-f780-4ebe-9df0-986b2d5960af","99556c04-24ce-46d5-8709-c2ec37c8b6f3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788416052117289001,"uuid":"e6378228-2f9e-4fb8-a9c0-24e35e197612"}